# Database Schema (Planned/Future)

**Note**: This schema represents the planned database structure for future backend integration. The mobile app currently uses local state management and mock data.

## Core Tables

### users
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
email: text (unique)
created_at: timestamp
```

### receipts
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
user_id: uuid (foreign key -> users.id)
store_name: text
store_chain: text
purchase_date: date
total_amount: decimal
receipt_image_url: text (Cloud storage URL - TBD)
created_at: timestamp
```

### receipt_items
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
receipt_id: uuid (foreign key -> receipts.id)
product_name_raw: text
normalized_product_id: uuid (foreign key -> products.id, nullable)
price: decimal
quantity: decimal
unit_price: decimal
created_at: timestamp
```

### products
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
name: text (normalized product name)
category: text
```

### product_aliases
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
alias_name: text (raw product name variations)
product_id: uuid (foreign key -> products.id)
```

**Example**: Aliases like "NORSK AGURK", "AGURK STK" map to normalized product "Agurk"

### stores
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
name: text
chain: text
location: text (optional)
```

**Store Chains**: Kiwi, Rema 1000, Coop Extra, Coop Prix, Coop Mega, Meny, Spar

### price_observations
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
product_id: uuid (foreign key -> products.id)
store_chain: text
store_name: text
price: decimal
timestamp: timestamp
receipt_id: uuid (foreign key -> receipts.id)
```

**Privacy**: Price observations are anonymized - user_id is NOT exposed in public queries.

### shopping_lists
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
user_id: uuid (foreign key -> users.id)
name: text
created_at: timestamp
```

### shopping_list_items
```sql
id: uuid (primary key)
list_id: uuid (foreign key -> shopping_lists.id)
product_id: uuid (foreign key -> products.id)
quantity: decimal
```

## Materialized Views

### product_prices_latest
```sql
product_id: uuid
store_chain: text
median_price: decimal
last_updated: timestamp
observation_count: integer
```

**Calculation Logic**:
- Median price from last 30 days
- Filter out price outliers
- Grouped by product_id and store_chain

